SCOPE (bead vms-0b6b / epic vms-da0, F1 of the GCC-as-VMS-oracle lane): this
bead needs GNU `as` (gas) plus the BFD/libiberty/opcodes it links — NOT gdb,
NOT ld, NOT gold, NOT the `binutils` driver-tools directory (ar/objcopy/
readelf/nm/strings/...), NOT gprof/gprofng. The upstream GNU FTP "binutils"
release tarball already excludes gdb/sim; this vendoring additionally
PRUNED, from the stock 2.43 release tree, the directories NOT needed to
build gas: gold/, ld/, gprof/, gprofng/, elfcpp/, binutils/ (the ar/objcopy/
readelf/nm/strings CLI tools directory — distinct from this
third-party/binutils/ vendor root; not a build dependency of gas). Also
pruned the DejaGNU test-fixture testsuite/ subdirectory of bfd/, gas/,
opcodes/ (gas/testsuite/ alone is 142M) — confirmed empirically (see below)
that none of the three sub-configure scripts (gas/configure, bfd/configure,
opcodes/configure) reference their own testsuite/ in AC_CONFIG_FILES, so
none is a build input for `make all-gas`.

CORRECTED DURING THE HOST-SIDE BUILD PROOF (this session): an initial, more
aggressive prune also dropped po/ (gettext catalogs) and doc/ (Texinfo
manuals) everywhere, and libctf/ entirely. Both turned out to be real build
inputs, not just optional artifacts:
  - gas/configure, bfd/configure and opcodes/configure each unconditionally
    list `po/Makefile.in:po/Make-in` in AC_CONFIG_FILES (regardless of
    --disable-nls) — config.status hard-fails ("cannot find input file:
    `po/Make-in'") without the (small) po/Make-in template and its gettext
    Makevars/POTFILES.in/*.sed/*.header/*.sin sidecar files. RESTORED po/ in
    full for bfd/, gas/, opcodes/ (~22M) rather than cherry-pick the exact
    subset make needs — cheap, and avoids a second round of "which gettext
    boilerplate file is it THIS time" discovery.
  - libiberty/configure lists `testsuite/Makefile` in AC_CONFIG_FILES
    unconditionally too — RESTORED libiberty/testsuite/ (172K, tiny; unlike
    gas's, libiberty's testsuite/ genuinely gates config.status).
  - `make all-gas` transitively builds all-libsframe (bfd's SFrame stack-
    trace section support), whose Makefile has a `doc/sframe-spec.info`
    rule depending on `doc/sframe-spec.texi` — RESTORED bfd/doc/, gas/doc/,
    libsframe/doc/ (~4.2M total; opcodes/ has no doc/ in the stock tree) so
    that rule has its input.
  - libsframe/sframe.c does `#include "swap.h"`, resolved via libctf/'s
    directory (a byte-swap helper header, not a CTF-specific one) —
    RESTORED libctf/ in full (2.1M) rather than lift the single header out
    of context.
All four corrections are documented here rather than silently applied — the
first prune attempt was WRONG (three separate configure-time hard failures,
reproduced and fixed in sequence during this bead's host-side build proof),
not a deliberate scope decision.

