To re-vendor at a new pin:
  curl -LO https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/binutils/binutils-<new-version>.tar.xz
  tar xf binutils-<new-version>.tar.xz
  cd binutils-<new-version> && rm -rf gold ld gprof gprofng elfcpp binutils
  rm -rf bfd/testsuite gas/testsuite opcodes/testsuite
  rsync -a --delete ./ third-party/binutils/src/
  # update the fields above with the new tarball name/date/sha256sum. Then
  # re-run the host-side proof (see mk_as.sh's header) to confirm
  # config.status still resolves cleanly at the new pin before committing —
  # this is exactly the check that caught the po/Make-in, libiberty
  # testsuite/Makefile.in, and libsframe doc/swap.h gaps above; a future
  # upstream release could add a new one.
